{"anchor": {"begin": [126, 0, 570.67], "end": [126, 0, 669.33], "env": "lemma", "file": null, "head": null, "id": 58, "kind": "approximate", "label": null, "labels": [], "line": null, "number": "A.1", "source_sha256": "e0034f5a74ab8c1d9caf6721799798d394fa78ee30323628a54ff62c9d0192d5", "statement": "Lemma A.1. Let α 1 , . . . , αm be distinct real numbers. For each j let β j be a nonnegative, nonzero smooth function supported in the interior of a compact interval I j ⊂ (0, ∞ ), with I 1 < · · · < I m . The matrix B ij = ∫︂ ∞ 0 xαi β j (x) dx is invertible. The assertion also holds for exponential weights in a logarithmic coordinate. If these data vary smoothly over a compact parameter set and the stated separations persist, the inverse and each fixed parameter derivative of it are bounded.", "title": null}, "blockers": [], "class": "proved", "clauses": [], "correspondence": {"by": "Christian Garry (drafted with Claude Code)", "confidence": "high", "coverage": "full", "note": "Split into the power-weight invertibility, the exponential (logarithmic-coordinate) version, and bounded parameter derivatives of the inverse on a compact set; the bumps need only be continuous and supported in [l_j, u_j] with u_i < l_j for i < j.", "source": "confirmed"}, "decls": {"NavierStokes.ExponentialMomentMatrix.expBumpMomentMatrix": "0f50fe600b72285d5bc6987b", "NavierStokes.PowerMomentMatrix.bumpMomentMatrix": "0cd14b894310dea9e86ce89a", "NavierStokes.SmoothPowerMomentMatrix.Family": "4888f24aee788215d93e51db", "NavierStokes.SmoothPowerMomentMatrix.Family.bump": "300828c22cee13688476d28f", "NavierStokes.SmoothPowerMomentMatrix.Family.exponent": "aded1c7d8dc26f1f63b573e1", "NavierStokes.SmoothPowerMomentMatrix.Family.matrix": "61bfdd466b31649bbf6dc13c", "NavierStokes.SmoothPowerMomentMatrix.Family.mk": "f42dfaa5fe6e5c98c4ebba2b"}, "findings": [], "heading": null, "id": "P:lemma-A.1", "key": "lemma-A.1", "kind": "lemma", "links": [{"axioms": ["propext", "Classical.choice", "Quot.sound"], 